  "claim_short": "For K_n = {x in G : n x = 0}, torsion gives G = union_n K_n. Each K_n is a closed subgroup. By the Baire category theorem, some K_N has nonempty interior and hence is open. The compact discrete quotient G/K_N is finite; if its exponent is q, then Nq annihilates all of G.",
